  "change": "Retain read-only command memory in SvgRoot and expose a span for replay. Ordinary filter capture and terminal offset/merge replay borrow slices instead of allocating and copying unchanged subtrees. Generated/rebound commands and geometry arrays remain independently admitted.",
  "ownership": "Borrowed views retain the same parent scene lifetime, geometry/resource indices and relative command indexing. They create no heap owner, scene reservation or command array. Recursive captures finish before parent disposal; genuine command rewrites retain their existing owner and cleanup. Bounds, maps, text layout, sampling and alpha stages are unchanged.",
  "regression": "Three Contract cases compare one versus 64 identical opaque draws under offset, blur and offset/merge. The larger retained scene must rasterize under the first scene's measured raster allowance, then pass existing peak-minus-one refusal, exact cancellation/cleanup and retry checks. Equal pixels support the contract relation; independent native banks separately own rendering correctness.",
